  [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m uses CommonJS [38;5;153mmodule.exports[39m and is only ever reached from Node via [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m. A shared validation
  module has to be reachable from the browser page, and ideally from Node so it can be tested without a browser. There's
  no bundler and no dependencies, so whatever we pick, we live with directly.

  - [1mES modules[0m — [38;5;153msrc/validation.js[39m uses [38;5;153mexport[39m, [38;5;153mindex.html[39m becomes [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m. Cleanest and the
    direction the ecosystem went. Costs: the page stops working when opened as a [38;5;153mfile://[39m URL (module scripts are
    CORS-restricted), so you'd need to serve it — [38;5;153mnpx serve[39m, [38;5;153mpython3 -m http.server[39m, anything. Also leaves [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m
    on CommonJS, so the repo has two styles until someone converts it.
  - [1mClassic global script[0m — [38;5;153msrc/validation.js[39m assigns [38;5;153mwindow.FormValidation[39m, and [38;5;153mindex.html[39m loads it before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m. Zero
    friction, [38;5;153mfile://[39m keeps working, matches how [38;5;153mapp.js[39m is written today. Costs: not importable from Node, so tests
    would need a DOM-ish shim or a hand-rolled global harness.
  - [1mDual CommonJS + global[0m — the file ends with a conditional [38;5;153mmodule.exports[39m / [38;5;153mwindow[39m assignment. Works in the browser
    as a plain script [3mand[0m imports cleanly in Node for tests. Costs: a few lines of boilerplate at the bottom that look
    dated.

  Cheap to change later: adding rules, the schema's shape. Expensive: this one — it decides whether [38;5;153mindex.html[39m needs a
  dev server, and whether tests can import the module at all. Converting later means touching the HTML and every
  consumer.

  [1mMy recommendation: dual CommonJS + global.[0m It's the only option that gets the module under test in Node without adding
  tooling, while leaving [38;5;153mindex.html[39m openable as a plain file exactly as it is now. The boilerplate is four lines and it
  buys the testability that makes a "reusable" module actually safe to reuse.
